We are walking slowly home from the beach.
It is almost twelve at night, but the sky is still light blue.
Nina, Eva, and Peter are walking next to me.
They are laughing and talking about the big bonfire.
I smile and listen to them.
"What are you thinking about, Maya?" Nina asks.
"I was thinking about my first day," I answer.
"I stepped off the plane six months ago," I say.
"It was very dark and cold in January," Peter laughs.
"Yes, but tonight the sky is bright," I say.
"And you have made some good friends," Eva smiles.
"Exactly," I say and look at them.
"I have built a wonderful life here," I continue.
We have had a fantastic evening together.
We cross the street and walk down our road.
I feel a very deep peace.
It is my birthday, and I am truly happy.
